# Kotlin Multiplatform Gradle Dependency Configuration

Based on the Ktor documentation provided, here's the complete dependency setup:

## Version Declaration
```gradle
[versions]
ktor = "3.4.0"
kotlinx-coroutines = "1.10.2"
```

## Library Definitions
```gradle
[libraries]
ktor-client-core = { module = "io.ktor:ktor-client-core", version.ref = "ktor" }
ktor-client-okhttp = { module = "io.ktor:ktor-client-okhttp", version.ref = "ktor" }
ktor-client-darwin = { module = "io.ktor:ktor-client-darwin", version.ref = "ktor" }
kotlinx-coroutines-core = { module = "org.jetbrains.kotlinx:kotlinx-coroutines-core", version.ref = "kotlinx-coroutines" }
kotlinx-coroutines-android = { module = "org.jetbrains.kotlinx:kotlinx-coroutines-android", version.ref = "kotlinx-coroutines" }
```

## SourceSet Configuration (shared/build.gradle.kts)
```gradle
sourceSets {
    commonMain.dependencies {
        implementation(libs.ktor.client.core)
        implementation(libs.kotlinx.coroutines.core)
    }
    androidMain.dependencies {
        implementation(libs.ktor.client.okhttp)
    }
    iosMain.dependencies {
        implementation(libs.ktor.client.darwin)
    }
}
```

## Android-Specific Setup (composeApp/build.gradle.kts)
```gradle
sourceSets {
    androidMain.dependencies {
        implementation(libs.kotlinx.coroutines.android)
    }
}
```

**Note:** The documentation does not include content negotiation or serialization libraries—only HTTP client core, platform-specific engines, and coroutines.
